# Context

## Background
T084 targeted P-APPLY, which failed both corpora while P-CHECKPOINT
passed on the same binary. The recorded failures came from a bench run
of commit fcac83e; the C2 record also carried correctness_oracle
"failed" because the harness probe read only the first 50-group diff
page of the 148-group comparison, so its plan restored a subset no
independent tree derivation could ever match.

## Why This Way
The untimed preparation step of P-APPLY already derives the pinned
review (the plan's review_id is only computable from the manifest), so
the timed review was re-deriving work the protocol had already paid
for. The cache removes the repetition without moving any production
work into untimed preparation: P-DIFF still clears the cache before
every timed run so that metric keeps measuring the cold derivation.

## Gotchas
- The git-invocation logging shim (a bash wrapper on PATH) costs about
  1.5 ms per Git process; at C1 that inflated a 0.37 s apply to 0.61 s.
  Phase timelines taken with the shim must subtract its overhead.
- `objects_present` answers Ok(false) on missing objects, so a cache
  miss rederives and the missing object fails the derivation typed —
  the pre-cache failure surface is preserved (failure_phases covers it).
- Entry files are lowercase hex names of the key OID; eviction treats
  any other name as not-an-entry and never deletes it.

